1
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:33,560
My name is Liu Xuemei.

2
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,520
I'm 32 years old.

3
00:00:35,719 --> 00:00:38,759
I'm a beer taster at State-Owned Lacheng Brewery.

4
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:40,880
As a beer taster,

5
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,039
our job is very important.

6
00:00:45,799 --> 00:00:47,880
I really like my coworkers.

7
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,520
They're like family to me.

8
00:00:50,719 --> 00:00:52,719
And I really like our brewery.

9
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,119
What else should I say?

10
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:57,280
Anything.

11
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,880
Say whatever's on your mind.

12
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,600
Talk about your dreams, your hobbies,

13
00:01:01,719 --> 00:01:02,679
your hopes for the factory.

14
00:01:03,039 --> 00:01:03,799
Anything at all.

15
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,359
I hope my son

16
00:01:07,439 --> 00:01:09,280
gets good grades on his final exams.

17
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:12,000
He's eight years old this year.

18
00:01:12,359 --> 00:01:14,079
I hope he gets into a good college someday.

19
00:01:14,239 --> 00:01:15,519
Good.

20
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:05,639
Master.

21
00:03:05,639 --> 00:03:06,319
Quick.

22
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,759
What's wrong?

23
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:12,439
Why are you being so cautious again?

24
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:14,039
Did something happen?

25
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:18,000
Why isn't Haipeng here yet?

26
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:19,159
I didn't ask him to come today.

27
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:22,719
Because last time,

28
00:03:23,439 --> 00:03:24,199
right in the middle of our chat,

29
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:25,000
the cops showed up.

30
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:26,680
We didn't get to finish what we were saying.

31
00:03:28,039 --> 00:03:28,800
These past couple of days,

32
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,759
I figured something out.

33
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:32,680
What is it?

34
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,159
A traitor.

35
00:03:35,439 --> 00:03:35,879
Trai--

36
00:03:39,039 --> 00:03:40,159
What traitor?

37
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,759
Look, Chen.

38
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:46,159
The money we pooled back then to buy the factory...

39
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,840
How did Ma Guowen find out about it?

40
00:03:48,319 --> 00:03:49,280
Someone definitely told him.

41
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,360
An informant.

42
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,080
Right.

43
00:03:54,919 --> 00:03:57,039
But that person definitely wasn't Liu Xuemei.

44
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,639
It's definitely not Xuemei.

45
00:04:01,159 --> 00:04:02,599
Then... who was it?

46
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,639
Shen Leshui.

47
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:07,719
Her?

48
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:10,639
Why didn't I think of that?

49
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:13,319
No wonder you didn't call Haipeng today.

50
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,560
I'm just guessing, but...

51
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,160
she knew Ma Guowen first,

52
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,920
and only got close to us later.

53
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:24,800
Right?

54
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,160
And in the end,

55
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:27,800
what happened to us,

56
00:04:27,959 --> 00:04:29,480
she didn't put any of it in her film.

57
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:31,879
Instead, she aired a cut that satisfied Ma Guowen.

58
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,560
She even won an award for it.

59
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,040
Everything worked out for them.

60
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:35,879
It's been over ten years, right?

61
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,240
Over ten years.

62
00:04:37,439 --> 00:04:38,639
The moment Ma Guowen talked about selling the factory,

63
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:39,680
she came back.

64
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,199
Aren't they in cahoots?

65
00:04:42,319 --> 00:04:42,879
Aren't they?

66
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,920
Master is right.

67
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,040
That day, right after she walked in,

68
00:04:46,199 --> 00:04:47,079
the cops came right in after her.

69
00:04:48,959 --> 00:04:50,399
You mean that time?

70
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:52,720
When she showed us that dark silhouette on her camera?

71
00:04:53,399 --> 00:04:54,120
You couldn't see anything.

72
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,000
That's right.

73
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:57,519
Could she have been fishing for info from us?

74
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,800
Exactly!

75
00:04:59,279 --> 00:05:00,120
Ever since she came back,

76
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,120
she's been chatting up all the old-timers one by one.

77
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:03,720
Even I was fooled by her.

78
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,240
I thought to myself,

79
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,399
"Look how much she cherishes old bonds."

80
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,360
Now I get it.

81
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,800
She was just fishing for information.

82
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,519
Master is right.

83
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,079
So what do you want to do?

84
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,120
Those videotapes...

85
00:05:20,839 --> 00:05:21,399
Get our hands on them.

86
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:25,240
The entire process of us buying the factory back then,

87
00:05:25,639 --> 00:05:26,439
she recorded all of it.

88
00:05:27,439 --> 00:05:28,240
In those tapes of hers,

89
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,680
there must be clues about that traitor.

90
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,319
Once we find this traitor,

91
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:34,079
we can clear Xuemei's name.

92
00:05:34,079 --> 00:05:34,439
Right.

93
00:05:37,439 --> 00:05:38,879
I... I think,

94
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,519
when dealing with her,

95
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,199
we can't just use brute force.

96
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,199
We need to be clever.

97
00:05:45,519 --> 00:05:46,439
I've already arranged everything.

98
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,519
Just follow Master's plan.

99
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,160
Tieping.

100
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,279
Testing the radio.

101
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:19,920
Zero-Two, Zero-Two.

102
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,000
Zero-Two, Zero-Two, this is Zero-One.

103
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,160
This is Zero-One. Do you copy?

104
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,079
Please respond.

105
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,279
Copy that.

106
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:27,920
Good, good.

107
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,920
Stand by. Stand by.

108
00:06:29,519 --> 00:06:30,120
The lights are off.

109
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,680
The lights went out.

110
00:06:35,279 --> 00:06:37,000
The... the hallway light is on.

111
00:06:37,319 --> 00:06:38,000
He's out.

112
00:06:40,079 --> 00:06:41,879
He's coming down, coming down, coming down!

113
00:06:54,439 --> 00:06:54,920
Master.

114
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,800
Target's out of the building.

115
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:06,519
Stay on him.

116
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:07,879
Copy that.

117
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,600
Zero-Two, Zero-Two.

118
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:33,600
This is Zero-One.

119
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,519
Do you copy? Come in.

120
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,240
Copy.

121
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,759
What's the target doing?

122
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,399
He's on foot right now.

123
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:42,959
Good.

124
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:44,839
Keep eyes on him.

125
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,079
Stay in touch.

126
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,480
Copy that.

127
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,480
Let's go.

128
00:08:27,319 --> 00:08:27,920
This door.

129
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:29,639
Three... 302.

130
00:08:34,799 --> 00:08:36,320
You even brought this?

131
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:38,519
Isn't it empty?

132
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,279
Someone still lives here?

133
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:42,480
Tu.

134
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,039
Yeah.

135
00:08:43,759 --> 00:08:44,320
Keep it down.

136
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,039
I had no idea.

137
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,240
You even know how to pick locks?

138
00:08:49,519 --> 00:08:50,200
That's nothing.

139
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,080
We were skilled workers, after all.

140
00:08:54,759 --> 00:08:55,440
Got it?

141
00:08:59,399 --> 00:09:00,000
Don't rush me.

142
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:00,799
I can't see.

143
00:09:01,919 --> 00:09:04,080
Go to the car and grab my reading glasses.

144
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,279
What do you need reading glasses for?

145
00:09:06,799 --> 00:09:07,320
I brought mine.

146
00:09:08,759 --> 00:09:09,440
Mine are +2.50.

147
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:10,759
Will that work?

148
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:13,000
Anything under +3.00 is totally useless.

149
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,799
+3.00 isn't enough?

150
00:09:22,519 --> 00:09:23,480
You do it. You do it.

151
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,000
Just stick it in.

152
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:25,960
I don't know how.

153
00:09:27,279 --> 00:09:28,240
Never done this before.

154
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:29,039
What?

155
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,759
Afraid of getting a criminal record?

156
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,080
Wh-What...

157
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:32,840
What criminal record?

158
00:09:33,399 --> 00:09:35,000
Why be so sneaky at a time like this? No way.

159
00:09:35,159 --> 00:09:36,000
Just stick it in,

160
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,679
and give it a twist.

161
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:39,840
Put on gloves.

162
00:09:40,399 --> 00:09:41,000
No fingerprints.

163
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:41,759
No need, no need.

164
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,480
I... I have gloves.

165
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,200
Leather ones, too.

166
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:49,799
Here, here.

167
00:09:49,799 --> 00:09:50,159
Give it to me.

168
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,039
See that?

169
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:51,399
Just...

170
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:51,840
All right, all right.

171
00:09:51,879 --> 00:09:52,279
Shove it in.

172
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,679
Yeah, got it.

173
00:10:01,919 --> 00:10:03,519
Old Cheng, get back here!

174
00:10:23,759 --> 00:10:24,360
Tu Chunyan!

175
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,080
Get out here!

176
00:10:25,519 --> 00:10:26,200
Who is it?

177
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,159
Come out!

178
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,639
What's your problem?

179
00:10:31,919 --> 00:10:33,200
You've gone way too far!

180
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,600
Dumping such a huge pile of trash at my door!

181
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:35,799
Good grief!

182
00:10:35,799 --> 00:10:37,840
Which eye saw me put it there?

183
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,440
If it wasn't you, then who? Me?

184
00:10:40,879 --> 00:10:41,320
Take it away!

185
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,440
This isn't mine!

186
00:10:43,799 --> 00:10:44,600
I'm opening it up.

187
00:10:44,879 --> 00:10:45,799
If it's not mine,

188
00:10:45,799 --> 00:10:46,919
you're gonna eat it!

189
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,000
Holy crap!

190
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,159
Are you a ghost?!

191
00:10:53,639 --> 00:10:54,399
Master! Master!

192
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,399
Shen Leshui is back home!

193
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,039
Master!

194
00:10:57,559 --> 00:10:58,960
Shen Leshui is back home!

195
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:00,840
Master!

196
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,399
Shen Leshui is back home!

197
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:05,679
Oh, good grief!

198
00:11:05,919 --> 00:11:07,159
Shen Leshui is back home, Old Cheng!

199
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:08,240
What are you doing here?

200
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:09,720
What are you doing here?

201
00:11:11,759 --> 00:11:12,320
Copy that.

202
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,519
I'm the traitor?

203
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:16,879
Where's the proof?

204
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,159
You broke into my place,

205
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,519
and got caught red-handed!

206
00:11:25,799 --> 00:11:26,759
Look at how old you are!

207
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:27,799
What are you all doing?

208
00:11:27,799 --> 00:11:29,120
I was wondering what all that rustling was.

209
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,559
Turns out you two were picking the lock!

210
00:11:32,679 --> 00:11:33,200
Zhao Haipeng,

211
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,480
did you know about this?

212
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,120
How would I know?

213
00:11:38,039 --> 00:11:39,559
Didn't you tell me to come over?

214
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,039
If you want to watch the tapes, just ask me for them.

215
00:11:44,519 --> 00:11:46,480
Did you really have to resort to underhanded tricks?

216
00:11:50,879 --> 00:11:51,360
Master,

217
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,080
Shen Leshui went home.

218
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,720
I'm heading to the rendezvous point to meet you now.

219
00:11:58,879 --> 00:11:59,480
Oh, great.

220
00:12:00,279 --> 00:12:01,519
Not only did you pick my lock,

221
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,159
you even had someone tail me.

222
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Look at Tieping,

223
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,039
and then you, Old Tian...

224
00:12:07,759 --> 00:12:09,000
How did you teach your apprentice?

225
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:15,919
Leshui,

226
00:12:18,919 --> 00:12:20,879
look at how old they are.

227
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,759
Besides, you're all old friends,

228
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:24,440
right?

229
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:25,759
This... this...

230
00:12:25,759 --> 00:12:27,039
There must be some misunderstanding.

231
00:12:27,879 --> 00:12:28,519
Let it go.

232
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,200
Cut them some slack.

233
00:12:30,759 --> 00:12:31,159
What do you say?

234
00:12:34,159 --> 00:12:35,200
Let it go, Leshui.

235
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,559
You're both practically bald.

236
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:40,120
If I haul you to the police station,

237
00:12:40,399 --> 00:12:42,039
it'll just cause trouble for the officers.

238
00:12:42,279 --> 00:12:43,519
As if they don't have enough to deal with.

239
00:12:47,879 --> 00:12:49,559
I'll pretend this never happened today.

240
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:51,080
Don't let it happen again.

241
00:12:52,759 --> 00:12:53,600
Never again, you hear?

242
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:56,840
All right.

243
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,159
Let me pour you some water.

244
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:02,559
You...

245
00:13:03,519 --> 00:13:04,519
That crooked reporter...

246
00:13:06,279 --> 00:13:07,399
about us buying the factory,

247
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:09,639
she didn't include any of it in the documentary.

248
00:13:10,559 --> 00:13:11,159
Think about it!

249
00:13:11,559 --> 00:13:13,840
From start to finish, she was the only one who profited.

250
00:13:14,279 --> 00:13:15,720
If not you, who else would we suspect?

251
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:25,080
Come on, Chen, are you ever gonna drop this?

252
00:13:31,039 --> 00:13:32,360
I couldn't help you back then,

253
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:33,960
and that's on me.

254
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,679
But from start to finish,

255
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,480
I never betrayed you.

256
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,399
Where are those tapes of yours?

257
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,240
There must be some secret in them.

258
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,240
The tapes were stolen!

259
00:13:45,919 --> 00:13:47,080
Zhao Haipeng knows about it.

260
00:13:47,919 --> 00:13:50,440
Didn't you ask him during your little secret meetups?

261
00:13:54,039 --> 00:13:56,000
So you don't even include me in group activities anymore?

262
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:58,720
What's that supposed to mean?

263
00:13:59,759 --> 00:14:01,279
So you two suspect me too, huh?

264
00:14:03,279 --> 00:14:03,879
No...

265
00:14:04,799 --> 00:14:05,399
Well...

266
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:06,879
Haipeng...

267
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,240
weren't you, you know...

268
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,679
We just didn't want you to, you know...

269
00:14:09,759 --> 00:14:10,879
What "you know"?

270
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:12,200
Busy.

271
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,080
You're busy, exactly.

272
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:14,840
Unbelievable, you guys.

273
00:14:15,559 --> 00:14:16,399
Well, we didn't know

274
00:14:16,759 --> 00:14:18,240
her tapes were stolen.

275
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,600
Who stole them?

276
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,039
What do you mean?

277
00:14:37,039 --> 00:14:38,080
Why are you all staring at me?

278
00:14:38,559 --> 00:14:39,480
Come on, this is ridiculous.

279
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,120
I live right across from her,

280
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:44,320
right?

281
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,559
I've only been to her place twice.

282
00:14:46,879 --> 00:14:47,639
Right, Shen Leshui?

283
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,200
Every time I came over, she was home.

284
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,399
I couldn't have stolen your tapes.

285
00:14:50,399 --> 00:14:50,720
Am I right?

286
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:51,639
Say something!

287
00:14:57,159 --> 00:14:58,919
I suspect Gao Xuelin stole them.

288
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:00,879
Who?

289
00:15:01,399 --> 00:15:04,039
That cop who came to Old Workers' Haven

290
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,159
